Pane fixtures for the turn-state read (adp_turn_running / adp_turn_state).

PROVENANCE MATTERS MORE THAN USUAL HERE, because the anchor these pin is a claim about what real
clients render. Eight of the nine are verbatim captures of real client TUIs, taken at 100 columns;
one is derived from a capture and says so. Machine- and change-specific text was replaced
(checkout path, PR number, model name, quota percentage) — rule zero. Nothing else was touched:
the leading codepoints, the line positions and where each marker sits are as captured, and those
are the only properties the anchor reads.

Why the anchor needs fixtures at all: a too-loose anchor restores the false `delivered` this
change exists to remove; a too-tight one makes a healthy running turn read as not-running, so the
commonest healthy path alarms and an operator learns to ignore the signal. Neither failure is
visible without real renders to measure against.

  pane-claude-running.txt        live, the first kind, mid-turn. Captured from a real supervised
                                 session's own pane over the agterm control socket. The turn
                                 marker is in the footer, which is the LAST non-empty line.
  pane-claude-idle.txt           live, same kind, idle at the composer. Same footer, no marker.
  pane-claude-draft.txt          live, same kind: a long directive TYPED BUT NOT SUBMITTED, so it
                                 wraps inside the composer. The marker is in the box, three lines
                                 above the footer. ADVERSARIAL: must read as not running.
  pane-claude-draft-welded.txt   live, same kind, the flattening case. Two fragments were typed as
                                 separate keystroke batches and the client rendered them as the
                                 intact marker inside the box — the shape `tr` welds together when
                                 a multi-line directive is flattened to one line. ADVERSARIAL.
                                 This is the case no earlier fixture had.
  pane-claude-queued.txt         live, same kind, a second message submitted while the first turn
                                 was still running. The client's queued hint is on the BOX line;
                                 the turn marker is simultaneously in the footer.
  pane-claude-content.txt        DERIVED, not a verbatim capture. Built from pane-claude-idle.txt
                                 by putting the marker into a line that frame already rendered as
                                 two-space-indented transcript text, and changing nothing else. It
                                 stands for a child displaying this plugin's own source, which is
                                 what permanently poisons a slot if the anchor is loose. The line's
                                 SHAPE is real; only its words are ours. ADVERSARIAL.
  pane-codex-running.txt         live, the second kind, mid-turn. This kind puts the marker in a
                                 column-one service line in the transcript flow, NOT in the
                                 footer — which is why the anchor needs two arms.
  pane-codex-idle.txt            live, same kind, idle at the composer.
  pane-codex-draft-welded.txt    live, same kind, typed-not-submitted and welded. ADVERSARIAL.

NOT CAPTURED, so not asserted: a queued render for the second kind. Its queued headers are known
from the client binary (read during review) but their placement on screen is not, so no fixture
claims it. If you add one, capture it rather than adapting the first kind's.
